confine-copy-feedback-to-footer

Lane: frontend

FlatPatch: confine-copy-feedback-to-footer

Form: GitDiff

Segment: snapshot

Purpose: Keep copy outcomes in the existing footer and mute selection hints above the composer without changing transcript or composer height.

Requires: none

Provides: Render native pending, busy, confirmed, unconfirmed and failed copy feedback in spare footer columns; preserve copy lifecycle and expiry, footer controls and warning hit targets, and gap navigation and links. Rendered-surface selection does not insert a Selecting text hint above the composer.

Boundary: Do not change clipboard delivery, selection and follow semantics, persistent status content, modal ownership, ordinary composer hints or bottom-pane row allocation. Keep complete copy outcome variants and omit them when no fitting space remains.

Verification: Focused owned-transcript mouse-copy and idle/running geometry tests, copy lifecycle and narrow rendering tests, footer content/cursor/warning-hit tests, and existing input and status footer coverage. Footer selection tests verify unchanged transcript cells and composer geometry through press, drag and release while preserving selected text, Escape and stationary warning clicks.


